Actually your muscle memory works against you in this game

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.320
but instead of leaving an embarrassing review on metacritic stick with it because

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.859
Honestly the combat could become your favorite of any

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:22.379
fromsoftware game like it has for me this video contains tips for those that are struggling and also,

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:27.060
Fascinating little details that I guarantee even the most seasoned player has missed

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.899
First did you know sekiro actually comes with

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:38.969
Difficulty settings? Finally right? After you defeat the chained ogre make a right at the samurai general and jump onto this branch

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:44.369
past the small hut look for a grabbable ledge move into the cave with headless in it and

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:47.609
Escape out the back to senpou temple ringing

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.099
This Bell curses you with increased difficulty

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.649
But it blesses you with increased item drops. Enemies actually don't become much harder,

00:00:56.079 --> 00:01:02.459
but bosses do so remove it before you fight a boss. Yeah, my first tip for new players is make the game harder!

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:10.470
But um hear me out because now that you have the Bell demon active for better crafting material drops we can talk about grinding

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:17.159
It's honestly something that I recommend every player does at least once because not only does it give you gold, experience,

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.890
extra healing items, and crafting materials

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:22.949
You'll hone your combat skills in a predictable environment

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.679
Which means that you'll actually see yourself become more efficient at taking out all of these enemies.

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:32.909
The best early game location for grinding is undoubtedly

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:39.298
I think the first stretch of the Hirata estates where enemies give 34 experience, 23 gold,

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:45.599
Pellets, and also rare crafting materials like scrap iron and even black gunpowder. Now

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.540
There are two items you absolutely should use up while grinding green and gold Mibu Balloons

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:57.479
Before you start killing enemies pop the green mibu balloon, which increases item drop rate

00:01:57.759 --> 00:01:58.420
however

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:03.629
Don't pick any of it up yet when you've finished killing your entire runs worth of enemies

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:10.050
Then pop the gold mibu balloon which increases gold acquisition and it actually applies retroactively

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.359
to all of the gold that you've left on the ground

00:02:13.519 --> 00:02:18.219
Which means you can run back through the area listen to the sweet sweet sound of gold

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:24.009
Clinking and then start a new run killing a few more enemies for gold before that balloon buff disappears

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.420
It's very efficient

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:31.750
This whole process should give you at least four experience points to spend and there are three skills

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.349
I consider to be baseline for anybody first

00:02:35.349 --> 00:02:40.089
There's mikiri in the shinobi art tree. There are tons of enemies that have

00:02:40.609 --> 00:02:42.609
devastating perilous thrust attacks and

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:49.810
By dashing towards them Mikiri gives you what is actually a very very forgiving option to completely

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:53.259
Nullify that damage and you also deal a bit of posture damage as well

00:02:53.840 --> 00:03:01.840
After this you can invest in suppressed presence which drastically improves your stealth next in the prosthetic art tree

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:06.908
Chasing slice a skill that's really really good with the shuriken arm

00:03:06.909 --> 00:03:13.119
And honestly, the shuriken is probably the best prosthetic for general combat. It's cheap,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.829
It allows you to interrupt enemies,

00:03:14.829 --> 00:03:20.049
It allows you to finish off weak enemies, and you can chain together combos and enemies really

00:03:20.329 --> 00:03:20.829
Really

00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:25.629
Well use this if you have a ton of gold and you're at a loss as to what to invest it in

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.399
You should always have options. The best option is gold pouches

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:36.310
These are consumable bags of your own money that prevent it being lost upon death

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.209
They cost about 10 percent of the gold that you spend on them

00:03:40.549 --> 00:03:46.959
But you will always get value from these considering you're gonna lose 50% of that gold if you die

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:53.679
So buy them whenever you see them, seriously, if you have nothing else to invest in you can buy spirit emblems

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:59.799
Which actually only cost 10 gold at the start of the game. When you do die you spread dragon rot.

00:03:59.799 --> 00:04:06.039
Which reduces your chance of receiving unseen aid. A lot of people ask me what type of death spreads dragon rot

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.760
So here's the answer only true death spreads dragon rot

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.989
If you die and resurrect that death does not spread dragon rot

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:17.768
If you ever feel that you might die because you're out of gourd or something

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:24.609
Just peace out instead every player now has a home wood Idol which unlike in previous games can be used to teleport you

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:28.629
Back to a checkpoint for free this way. You won't lose half your experience

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:35.110
You can invest your gold and those around you won't get dragon cancer if your quickselect bar ever starts to feel cluttered

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:41.800
Remember holding down left or right on the d-pad will immediately skip you to the first item on your bar

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.960
Which should always be your healing gourd.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:52.480
Honestly, I'd recommend you only ever keep gourd and pellets on your bar the rest are items that you can just use situationally in the

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.170
pause menu and

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.920
Pellets are really good. You get a ton of them throughout the game

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:03.099
Of course, you may not like where your buttons are for heal, and I can't blame you the controls are bit strange

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:07.869
However, everyone can now rebind buttons at will and most players

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.380
I think will prefer having triangle or Y as heal and

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:19.450
Up on the d-pad to switch prosthetic weapons instead this lets you move around with the left thumbstick and heal at the same time

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:26.349
Speaking of button presses. Have you ever wondered what happens if you don't take the second R one deathblow offered on main bosses?

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:31.629
This happens if you ever died an embarrassing amount to a boss

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:39.009
Looking at you lady butterfly. Now you can show them what it's like to die over and over again one button

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:41.650
That I guarantee most of you haven't pressed is

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.569
Triangle or Y when you're in the travel screen this opens up an antique map

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:51.189
Which is this beautiful little piece of art that expands as you explore more areas

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.679
But in order to explore that map

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:59.530
You're going to have to be good at combat and to follow here are 10 powerful

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.799
underappreciated mechanics that exist in combat

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:09.549
These are things that struggling players need to know and that even experienced players might be overlooking. First

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:16.179
consider resetting stealth if you get spotted hop a few fences stay out of line of sight for a little while and

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:23.560
Sometimes with enemies like the chained Ogre, for example, they'll actually turn their back on you as they return to their standing point

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:31.210
Which puts them in a position where a stealth kill is possible where usually they weren't even possible before this strategy works pretty well

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.540
Against mini bosses like the Shinobi hunter or Juzou

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:41.380
Bosses that have a ton of smaller enemies that you're going to want to stealth kill one at a time before engaging them

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:48.519
Now while stealth can get pretty cheesy combat is anything but these first few days have been full of souls fans

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:55.810
Realizing that they can't get away with dodge r1 anymore. I do want to confirm though. Yes, I frames do exist

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.320
they exist on jumps and they exist on Dodges, but

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:02.260
enemies now have far far better tracking

00:07:02.389 --> 00:07:09.249
Because you're supposed to be deflecting these attacks in a way most attacks are supposed to track you and hit you so

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.149
Don't dodge through them. This is a game about clashing swords

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:17.380
And the only time you should be spacing enemies is when they do perilous attacks

00:07:17.479 --> 00:07:19.839
Or if you're facing multiple enemies

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:21.350
standing face-to-face

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:28.839
With an enemy is no longer a dangerous position to be in and a mountain of positive effects are baked into blocking

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.859
Let me show you them what you're seeing here is attack cancelling

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:36.999
Enabling a block as long as the actual swing isn't in motion

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:43.479
This is why it's important not to spam r1 attacks. Like you can in Souls games. This will queue your attacks

00:07:43.479 --> 00:07:48.519
You'll do more than you intend to and it'll make it harder to block cancel instead

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:55.299
Consciously tap r1 once every time you attack so that you're always fully in control this way

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:01.930
Your enemy will eventually power through your assault and you will be ready to start blocking at a moment's notice

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:08.560
Few new players understand just how powerful a tool blocking is it prevents all damage

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.720
It can be used to inflict posture damage

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:18.160
It comes out at a moment's notice and you can also recover posture twice as fast while blocking. Look at this

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:22.419
So if you don't need to move out of the way of anything, and you're just waiting

00:08:22.849 --> 00:08:29.229
block should be your standard position and a super OP technique that few people are utilizing is

00:08:30.139 --> 00:08:37.299
Repeatedly tapping block as fast as you can while being attacked it repeats so fast that it's actually impossible

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:43.390
To get hit through it and it also gives you a decent chance at deflecting a blow

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.230
Don't do this all the time

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:50.140
Obviously you still have to think but if you have a feeling overwhelmed by a flurry of attacks

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:55.330
You can just spam that block and try to keep up with them at best

00:08:55.330 --> 00:09:00.549
You deflect some attacks at worst your posture gets overwhelmed and bear in mind

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:04.870
Most enemies can't even necessarily capitalize on breaking your posture

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:08.560
So you might not even take damage if you roll fast enough

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:14.259
Another reason spam tapping is important is because of another mechanic called consecutive

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:19.660
Deflect which increases the posture damage you do for deflecting multiple hits in a row

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:25.150
Many enemies have flurry attacks. These are attacks that are a huge opportunity for you

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:29.140
You want to see flurry attacks seeing the pacing in your head

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:35.200
For example, this enemy is one two, three, four. One, two, three, four, five one

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:39.099
And now I'm actually happy to see this attack coming my way

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:43.150
Sekiro is in no small way a rhythm game

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:48.039
If you do take an unblocked hit you'll actually notice your character falling off balance

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:53.500
This stumble can be resolved by blocking or dodging and as you can probably guess

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:55.010
Blocking is better

00:09:55.010 --> 00:10:01.330
Your recovery is actually immediate if you turn it into a deflect enemies can get perfect deflects as well

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.359
And while they don't reduce your posture

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:12.039
They do affect the flow of your attacks giving you a brief pause and putting you back to the first attack in your sequence

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.400
Enemies can use this pause to launch a combo of their own

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:20.260
So if you notice them starting their own combo just let it happen go on

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:24.789
the defensive combat is now about trading offense and defense and

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.150
defense is just as big an opportunity as

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:33.640
Offense is another opportunity. You're probably not making use of is your jump kick

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:39.310
So basically any enemy can be double jumped on enabling a tiny bit of damage with a double r1

00:10:39.589 --> 00:10:46.659
but something that most players overlook is that you actually deal a ton of posture damage if you jump kick a

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:48.999
Perilous sweep attack look at this

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:54.699
So next time you intuitively jump away from an enemy jump on them instead

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:59.470
Finally posture is linked to your health when a posture bar is glowing red

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:04.929
It means health is low and posture will regenerate slowly to kill most of the later bosses in the game

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.930
You actually have to be very aware of opportunities

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:12.910
That allow you to deal health damage because posture damage at the beginning of the fight is going to be worthless

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:17.650
One such example of this is against lady butterfly who suffers greatly

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.290
against repeated dodge attacks and

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:25.840
Shuriken throws when she's jumping between wires if you're appreciative of any of these tips

